  "title": "Collaborative rule learning promotes interbrain information alignment",
  "description": "This dataset contains EEG recordings from 24 pairs of participants performing a 4-way categorisation task based on rules they first agreed upon together. Participants also completed pre- and post-tests on the same stimuli. The data were collected to investigate how collaborative rule learning promotes information alignment between interacting brains.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded simultaneously from 24 pairs of participants during a collaborative 4-way categorisation task following joint rule agreement, with pre- and post-test sessions using the same stimuli. The experiment lasted approximately 1 hour.",
